<article class="env-remark" id="01ZG">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01ZG">Remark <span data-tag="01ZG">5.5.1.11</span>.</a> For every simplicial category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\circ }$ denote the underlying ordinary category of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ (Example <a data-tag="00JU" href="/tag/00JU">2.4.1.4</a>). Then we have canonical isomorphisms </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  ( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\triangleleft } )^{\circ } \simeq (\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\circ })^{\triangleleft } \quad \quad ( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\triangleright } )^{\circ } \simeq (\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\circ })^{\triangleright }, \]
</div>
<p> where the left hand sides are defined using Notation <a data-tag="01ZD" href="/tag/01ZD">5.5.1.8</a> and Variant <a data-tag="01ZE" href="/tag/01ZE">5.5.1.9</a>, and the right hand sides are defined in Example <a data-tag="0165" href="/tag/0165">4.3.2.5</a>. In other words, the formation of cones is compatible with the forgetful functor from simplicial categories to ordinary categories. </p>
</article>
